<!DOCTYPE html><html lang="en"><head><meta charSet="utf-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"/><link rel="preload" as="image" href="/images/ThePoolLab.png"/><link rel="stylesheet" href="/_next/static/css/d071dca61fbb01bf.css" crossorigin="" data-precedence="next"/><link rel="stylesheet" href="/_next/static/css/0fc6c400c3ed5371.css" crossorigin="" data-precedence="next"/><link rel="preload" as="script" fetchPriority="low" href="/_next/static/chunks/webpack-9104c05f1a1687bc.js" crossorigin=""/><script src="/_next/static/chunks/fd9d1056-4dbbcf07a05c3f48.js" async="" crossorigin=""></script><script src="/_next/static/chunks/472-6eced84fcf03e6a3.js" async="" crossorigin=""></script><script src="/_next/static/chunks/main-app-ce281d8555633725.js" async="" crossorigin=""></script><script src="/_next/static/chunks/326-bff252670b7455ef.js" async=""></script><script src="/_next/static/chunks/app/blog/%5Bslug%5D/page-c4cb47b92a816131.js" async=""></script><script src="/_next/static/chunks/975-95592eb349967368.js" async=""></script><script src="/_next/static/chunks/app/layout-4ee2f436a51b65f2.js" async=""></script><title>Dolphin Nautilus CC Plus vs Dolphin Premier: Which One Is Worth It? - The Pool Lab</title><meta name="description" content="The Dolphin Nautilus CC Plus and Dolphin Premier are two of the most popular robotic pool cleaners on the market. Compare cleaning performance, filtration, wall climbing, maintenance, and value to determine which model is best for your pool."/><link rel="canonical" href="https://www.the-pool-lab.com/blog/dolphin-nautilus-cc-plus-vs-dolphin-premier"/><meta property="og:title" content="Dolphin Nautilus CC Plus vs Dolphin Premier: Which One Is Worth It?"/><meta property="og:description" content="The Dolphin Nautilus CC Plus and Dolphin Premier are two of the most popular robotic pool cleaners on the market. Compare cleaning performance, filtration, wall climbing, maintenance, and value to determine which model is best for your pool."/><meta property="og:type" content="article"/><meta property="article:published_time" content="2026-02-09"/><meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image"/><meta name="twitter:title" content="The Pool Lab - Your ultimate guide to Robot Pool Cleaners, reviews, and maintenance tips."/><meta name="twitter:description" content="Your ultimate guide to Robot Pool Cleaners, reviews, and maintenance tips."/><meta name="twitter:image" content="https://www.the-pool-lab.com/images/ThePoolLabOG.png"/><script src="/_next/static/chunks/polyfills-c67a75d1b6f99dc8.js" crossorigin="" noModule=""></script></head><body class="d-flex flex-column min-vh-100"><nav class="navbar navbar-expand-lg navbar-light bg-light"><div class="container"><a class="navbar-brand d-flex align-items-center" href="/"><div style="width:160px;height:90px;position:relative;margin-right:10px"><img src="/images/ThePoolLab.png" alt="The Pool Lab Logo" style="width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:contain"/></div><span class="d-none d-sm-inline">The Pool Lab</span></a><button class="navbar-toggler" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#navbarNav"><span class="navbar-toggler-icon"></span></button><div class="collapse navbar-collapse" id="navbarNav"><ul class="navbar-nav ms-auto"><li class="nav-item"><a class="nav-link" href="/">Home</a></li><li class="nav-item"><a class="nav-link" href="/reviews">Reviews</a></li><li class="nav-item"><a class="nav-link" href="/best-of">Best of</a></li><li class="nav-item"><a class="nav-link" href="/guides">Guides</a></li><li class="nav-item"><a class="nav-link" href="/about">About</a></li></ul></div></div></nav><main class="flex-grow-1"><div class="container my-5"><nav aria-label="breadcrumb"><ol class="breadcrumb"><li class="breadcrumb-item"><a href="/">Home</a></li><li class="breadcrumb-item active" aria-current="page">Blog</li></ol></nav><article><h1 class="mb-4">Dolphin Nautilus CC Plus vs Dolphin Premier: Which One Is Worth It?</h1><p class="text-muted mb-5">Posted on <!-- -->2026-02-09</p><div class="row"><div class="col-lg-8"><div><h2>Dolphin Nautilus CC Plus vs Dolphin Premier: Quick Verdict</h2><p>The <strong><a href="/reviews/Dolphin-Nautilus-CC-Plus">Dolphin Nautilus CC Plus</a></strong> and <strong><a href="/reviews/Dolphin-Premier">Dolphin Premier</a></strong> are two of the most popular robotic pool cleaners in the Dolphin lineup. While they share the same goal—automating pool cleaning—they approach the task differently.</p><p>For most pool owners, the <strong>Dolphin Nautilus CC Plus</strong> represents the better overall value. It delivers strong floor and wall cleaning, simple operation, and a lower purchase price. The <strong>Dolphin Premier</strong>, on the other hand, is designed for buyers who want greater filtration flexibility and enhanced debris handling, particularly in pools that collect large amounts of leaves and seasonal debris.</p><p>If you simply want a dependable robotic cleaner that performs well with minimal fuss, the Nautilus CC Plus is often the safer choice. If your pool regularly battles leaves, acorns, seed pods, or mixed debris throughout the year, the Premier's filtration system may justify its higher price.</p><h2>At-a-Glance Comparison</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Dolphin Nautilus CC Plus</th><th>Dolphin Premier</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Best For</td><td>Most pool owners</td><td>Heavy debris environments</td></tr><tr><td>Value</td><td>Excellent</td><td>Moderate</td></tr><tr><td>Wall Cleaning</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>Filtration Options</td><td>Simple</td><td>Multiple configurations</td></tr><tr><td>Ease of Use</td><td>Very Easy</td><td>Moderate</td></tr><tr><td>Maintenance</td><td>Low</td><td>Moderate</td></tr><tr><td>Typical Buyer</td><td>Value-focused</td><td>Feature-focused</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>Cleaning Performance</h2><p>When evaluating robotic pool cleaners, cleaning performance matters more than feature lists. Fortunately, both models perform well in the areas that matter most.</p><p>The Nautilus CC Plus has built a strong reputation because it consistently removes common pool debris without requiring much intervention. It navigates efficiently, climbs walls effectively, and handles routine maintenance cleaning with minimal setup.</p><p>The Premier also delivers strong cleaning performance, but its advantage comes from adaptability. Pools experience different debris challenges throughout the year. Spring pollen, summer dirt, and fall leaves place different demands on filtration systems. The Premier's interchangeable filtration options allow owners to customize cleaning performance for changing conditions.</p><p>For pools that primarily collect dust, insects, and occasional leaves, many owners may never notice a meaningful cleaning difference between the two robots. In heavy leaf environments, however, the Premier's flexibility can become a significant advantage.</p><h2>Filtration Systems</h2><p>Filtration is arguably the biggest distinction between these two models.</p><p>The Nautilus CC Plus follows a simpler philosophy. It focuses on ease of ownership and straightforward maintenance. Owners spend less time deciding which filter configuration to use and more time simply running the robot.</p><p>The Premier takes the opposite approach. Rather than offering one generalized filtration strategy, it allows users to select filtration options based on the debris currently entering the pool.</p><p>This flexibility appeals to pool owners who deal with highly variable debris loads throughout the year. A pool surrounded by mature trees may require different filtration solutions during fall than during summer.</p><p>The tradeoff is complexity. More options generally mean more decisions and slightly more maintenance responsibility.</p><h2>Wall Climbing and Waterline Cleaning</h2><p>Many robotic pool cleaner buyers focus heavily on wall climbing ability. A robot that only cleans the floor often leaves significant dirt and algae buildup elsewhere.</p><p>Both the Nautilus CC Plus and the Premier are capable of cleaning walls. Their ability to maintain traction on vertical surfaces allows them to remove debris that would otherwise remain untouched.</p><p>Waterline cleaning performance can vary depending on pool shape, surface material, and debris conditions, but both models are generally considered capable wall climbers within the Dolphin product family.</p><p>If wall cleaning is one of your primary requirements, either model should satisfy most residential pool owners.</p><h2>Ease of Ownership</h2><p>Many pool owners underestimate how important daily usability becomes after purchase.</p><p>A robotic pool cleaner may run several times per week during peak swimming season. Small inconveniences accumulate quickly.</p><p>This is where the Nautilus CC Plus earns much of its popularity. Its design emphasizes simplicity. There are fewer decisions to make, fewer adjustments to manage, and fewer opportunities for user error.</p><p>The Premier requires slightly more involvement from the owner because of its expanded filtration system. Some pool owners appreciate this level of control, while others simply want to drop a robot into the water and let it work.</p><p>If convenience is your highest priority, the Nautilus CC Plus generally has the advantage.</p><h2>Long-Term Value</h2><p>Value should not be confused with price.</p><p>The cheapest robot is not always the best value, and the most expensive robot is not automatically the best performer.</p><p>The Nautilus CC Plus consistently appears on best-value lists because it delivers strong cleaning performance without requiring premium-level investment. For many pool owners, it occupies the sweet spot between capability and affordability.</p><p>The Premier can absolutely provide value as well, but that value is more dependent on individual circumstances. Owners who benefit from its filtration flexibility may consider the higher purchase price worthwhile. Others may find themselves paying for features they rarely use.</p><p>If value is your primary concern, you may also want to review our <a href="/best-of/value">Best Value Robotic Pool Cleaners</a> recommendations, which compare several top-performing models across different budgets.</p><h2>Who Should Buy the Dolphin Nautilus CC Plus?</h2><ul><li>Pool owners seeking maximum value.</li><li>Buyers who prioritize simplicity.</li><li>Pools with typical residential debris loads.</li><li>Owners who want strong wall cleaning without premium pricing.</li><li>Anyone looking for a reliable all-around robotic cleaner.</li></ul><h2>Who Should Buy the Dolphin Premier?</h2><ul><li>Pools surrounded by trees.</li><li>Owners dealing with seasonal debris variation.</li><li>Buyers who want multiple filtration options.</li><li>Users who appreciate customization and flexibility.</li><li>Pool owners willing to spend more for additional capability.</li></ul><h2>Final Recommendation</h2><p>For the majority of residential pool owners, the <strong>Dolphin Nautilus CC Plus</strong> is the better overall purchase. It delivers excellent cleaning performance, dependable wall climbing, simple maintenance, and strong value.</p><p>The <strong>Dolphin Premier</strong> remains an excellent robotic cleaner, particularly for pools that experience significant debris loads throughout the year. Its advanced filtration flexibility gives it an edge in challenging environments, but that advantage comes at a higher price and with additional complexity.</p><p>If you're unsure which robot fits your situation, the Nautilus CC Plus is typically the safer recommendation. If debris management is your biggest challenge, the Premier deserves serious consideration.</p><h2>Related Resources</h2>

<ul>
<li><a href="/reviews/Dolphin-Nautilus-CC-Plus">Dolphin Nautilus CC Plus Review</a></li>
<li><a href="/reviews/Dolphin-Premier">Dolphin Premier Review</a></li>
<li><a href="/best-of/overall">Best Robotic Pool Cleaners</a></li>
<li><a href="/best-of/value">Best Value Robotic Pool Cleaners</a></li>
</ul><h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2><h3>Is the Dolphin Premier worth the extra money?</h3><p>It depends on your pool environment. Owners with heavy leaf loads or seasonal debris often benefit most from the Premier's filtration flexibility. For many residential pools, the Nautilus CC Plus provides better overall value.</p><h3>Which cleaner is easier to maintain?</h3><p>The Nautilus CC Plus is generally easier to maintain because of its simpler filtration system and straightforward operation.</p><h3>Do both models clean walls?</h3><p>Yes. Both the Nautilus CC Plus and Dolphin Premier are capable wall-climbing robotic pool cleaners designed to clean both floors and walls.</p><h3>Which cleaner is better for leaves?</h3><p>The Dolphin Premier often receives the advantage in leaf-heavy environments due to its flexible filtration options and ability to adapt to changing debris conditions.</p><h3>Which model is best for most pool owners?</h3><p>For most residential pool owners, the Dolphin Nautilus CC Plus offers the strongest combination of performance, simplicity, and value.</p></div><div class="mt-5"><a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" href="/reviews">Find Your Perfect Robot</a></div></div></div></article></div></main><footer class="bg-dark text-white text-center py-3 mt-auto"><div class="container"><p class="mb-1">© <!-- -->2026<!-- --> <!-- -->The Pool Lab<!-- -->. All rights reserved.</p><small class="text-white-50">The Pool Lab<!-- --> is a participant in the Amazon Services LLC Associates Program, an affiliate advertising program designed to provide a means for sites to earn advertising fees by advertising and linking to Amazon.com.</small></div></footer><script src="/_next/static/chunks/webpack-9104c05f1a1687bc.js" crossorigin="" async=""></script><script>(self.__next_f=self.__next_f||[]).push([0]);self.__next_f.push([2,null])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"1:HL[\"/_next/static/css/d071dca61fbb01bf.css\",\"style\",{\"crossOrigin\":\"\"}]\n2:HL[\"/_next/st